    "abstract": "The paper decomposes robust error into natural error plus boundary error and derives a tight differentiable upper bound using classification-calibrated surrogate losses. This motivates TRADES, which minimises natural cross-entropy plus a regulariser (weighted by 1/lambda) pushing the decision boundary away from data via KL divergence between clean and adversarial predictions. TRADES won the NeurIPS 2018 Adversarial Vision Challenge.",
    "domain": "CV",
    "key_claims": [
      "Robust error decomposes into natural error and boundary error, with a tight upper bound in terms of surrogate losses.",
      "TRADES minimises CE(f(X), Y) + (1/lambda) max KL(f(X) || f(X')) over an eps-ball, trading off accuracy and robustness.",
      "On CIFAR-10 with WRN-34-10 and eps=0.031, TRADES (1/lambda=6) attains 84.92% natural and 56.61% robust accuracy under FGSM^k (PGD-20).",
      "TRADES won first place in the NeurIPS 2018 Adversarial Vision Challenge (robust model track)."
    ],
    "parsed_at": "2026-10-23T12:00:00+05:30",
